 ],
 "text": "If you tried to jump from New York to London, you'd land about 9 meters away, still in Times Square. Now, if you built a ramp off the top of the Empire State Building and left it at 26,000 km an hour, you'd clear the Atlantic in about 15 minutes, wave at a cruise ship, and land in London about 18 minutes later. Before you touch the ground, it starts raining, and the flight would have been cheaper."
